---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Pipeline from '../components/Pipeline.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Pipeline"
	eyebrow="[ 03 · PIPELINE ]"
	description="From Contract ID to execution evidence — the end-to-end Kuyfi flow."
>
	<Pipeline />

	<h2>Step by step</h2>

	<h3>01 · INPUT — Contract ID</h3>
	<p>
		You provide a Soroban Contract ID (<code>C</code> + 55 characters). Validation is shared
		between TUI and CLI via <code>isValidContractId()</code>. A malformed ID fails before any
		RPC work (and before any paid quote on the HTTP API).
	</p>

	<h3>02 · OSINT SCANNER — Fetch WASM / specification</h3>
	<p>
		Read-only RPC: <code>getContractWasmByContractId</code>. No transactions are broadcast.
		The scanner compiles the bytecode, reads the <code>contractspecv0</code> custom section,
		and parses XDR entries with an alignment-tolerant loop.
	</p>

	<h3>03 · RECONSTRUCT — Attack surface</h3>
	<p>
		Output: function names, typed parameters, return presence, and a UDT registry
		(structs / unions / enums). This is everything Chaos Monkey needs to generate
		type-correct values — still without Rust source.
	</p>

	<h3>04 · CHAOS MONKEY — Type-aware vectors</h3>
	<p>
		Five vector families (math, access-control, call-order, fee/BPS, liquidity). Values are
		<strong>type-correct, not semantically valid</strong>: a random Address is not a funded
		admin. Attacks vary <em>one variable at a time</em> so failures can be attributed.
	</p>

	<h3>05 · SIMULATE — Simulate and classify</h3>
	<p>
		Every vector is simulated (preflight) first. If simulation fails, Kuyfi classifies from
		<code>DiagnosticEvent</code> traces and sends nothing. If it succeeds, assemble → sign
		with an ephemeral Friendbot key → broadcast to Testnet → poll → classify.
	</p>

	<h3>06 · OUTPUT — JSON / PDF report</h3>
	<p>
		One <code>SecurityReport</code> (<code>schemaVersion: "1.0.0"</code>). JSON and PDF are
		renders of the same object — same <code>reportId</code>, findings, and evidence.
	</p>

	<Callout type="info" title="UI ≠ engine">
		<p>
			TUI screens only call into <code>source/modules/</code>. The headless CLI uses the
			identical scanner / chaos_monkey / security_report / report_export path — zero
			duplication of audit logic.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<pre><code>Contract ID
    ↓
OSINT Scanner            fetch + decode WASM
    ↓
Attack Surface           functions, params, UDTs
    ↓
Chaos Monkey             type-aware fuzzing
    ↓
Trace Classification     DiagnosticEvent taxonomy
    ↓
SecurityReport           JSON / PDF</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
